# Site Maps

#### A **sitemap** shows how webpages are organized and connected. It helps us see the big picture of how users move through a site. 
 

<img src="https://images.code.org/3c891d019252e0106b3979e97851f3be-image-1761147296181.png" alt="design process graph of the cycle" width="550px" style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">


---


## 💼Career Connection: UX Designer

<img src="https://images.code.org/9731158db44349372b96a62c34b7e031-image-1760992932803.png" 
     alt="icon of a person working on the UX of a website" 
     style="width: 10%; border-radius: 5px; margin: 0px 20px 20px 10px; float: left;">

#### A **User Experience (UX) Designer** ensures a website is usable, enjoyable, and accessible for its intended users.

#### They research user needs, test designs, and create layouts that improve how people interact with websites and apps.

---

#### Your students will create a sitemap and trace user flow using sketch lab  and then use AI to build a quick app based on their flow. 


